Author: cqls <aaa@designconsultancy.co.uk>
Date:   Wed Sep 2 22:17:18 2026 +0100

    424 round 2: BorderKeyed was measuring BFS reachability, not final alpha — the fail-closed guard could not tell a 0% success from a 100% success

    Found live by the bugfix_420_417 lane's dynamic testing (CONTRIB round 3,
    folded into bugs_open/424), not by this session — verified against the
    actual code before fixing, not taken on trust.

    BorderKeyed's own doc comment always said "the fraction of border pixels
    that ended up fully transparent", but the code computed it from
    keyedByBorder — whether BFS reached a pixel within `outer` — which is
    eligibility for keying, not the result of it. A uniform border sitting
    anywhere in the graded band (reachable, but nowhere near `inner`) marked
    every border pixel "keyed" while none of them actually got alpha 0. Measured
    live: a 0.0%-actually-transparent failure and an 87.4%-actually-transparent
    success both read BorderKeyed=1.000 on the old code — the fail-closed guard
    in dynamic_adapter.go (unchanged; it was always checking the right field,
    just fed the wrong number) could not distinguish them.

    Fixed by tracking each pixel's FINAL alpha through the grading pass and
    computing the border stat from that (alpha==0), not from BFS reachability.
    New test TestKeyOutBackground_GradedBorderIsNotBorderKeyed reproduces the
    exact reported shape (a mid-band uniform border) and is mutation-proven: it
    FAILS against the reinstated pre-fix computation (confirmed by temporarily
    restoring it, running the test, and reverting — not committed, per the
    git-stash ban on this tree) and passes against the fix.

    Also noted for follow-up, not fixed here: the same live testing found a
    residual magenta fringe at the mark edge on an otherwise-successful
    generation (despill incomplete at the graded band) — recorded in NOTES, not
    chased blind without the actual image.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0167HQq4yQnBeJ6fxtGvwLdK

diff --git a/internal/adapters/imagegenerator/keyground.go b/internal/adapters/imagegenerator/keyground.go
